# Vercel Speed Insights Configuration Report

## Summary
Vercel Speed Insights has been successfully verified and is already properly configured in this project.

## What Was Done

### 1. Fetched Latest Documentation
- Retrieved the latest Vercel Speed Insights quickstart guide from: https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart
- Confirmed the project follows the official HTML/vanilla JavaScript integration pattern

### 2. Verified Package Installation
- Package: `@vercel/speed-insights` version `^2.0.0` (latest)
- Status: ✅ Already installed in package.json
- All dependencies are up to date with no security vulnerabilities

### 3. Verified HTML Integration
The Speed Insights tracking code is correctly implemented in both HTML files:

#### index.html
- ✅ Window stub function: `window.si = window.si || function () { (window.siq = window.siq || []).push(arguments); };`
- ✅ Script tag: `<script defer src="/_vercel/speed-insights/script.js"></script>`
- Location: Added in the `<head>` section

#### gallery.html
- ✅ Window stub function: `window.si = window.si || function () { (window.siq = window.siq || []).push(arguments); };`
- ✅ Script tag: `<script defer src="/_vercel/speed-insights/script.js"></script>`
- Location: Added in the `<head>` section

### 4. Framework Verification
- Project Type: Vanilla HTML/CSS/JavaScript
- Integration Method: HTML script injection (as per Vercel docs for HTML projects)
- Implementation: Matches the official documentation exactly

### 5. Dependencies Status
- Ran `npm install` to verify all dependencies
- All packages are current and secure (0 vulnerabilities)
- Lock file (package-lock.json) is up to date

## Configuration Details

The project follows the Vercel Speed Insights quickstart guide for HTML projects:

1. **Package Installation**: The `@vercel/speed-insights` package is installed as a dependency
2. **Script Stub**: Both HTML files include the required window.si stub function
3. **Tracking Script**: Both HTML files load the Speed Insights script from `/_vercel/speed-insights/script.js`
4. **Defer Attribute**: Scripts are loaded with the `defer` attribute for optimal performance

## How Speed Insights Works

Once deployed to Vercel:
- Speed Insights will automatically track Core Web Vitals (LCP, FID, CLS, FCP, TTFB)
- Performance data will be available in the Vercel dashboard under "Speed Insights"
- The tracking script appears at `/_vercel/speed-insights/script.js` after deployment
- Data becomes available after several user visits to the site

## Next Steps

1. **Enable Speed Insights in Vercel Dashboard**:
   - Navigate to your Vercel project dashboard
   - Select "Speed Insights" from the sidebar
   - Click the "Enable" button for your project

2. **Deploy the Project**:
   - Run `vercel deploy` or push to your connected Git repository
   - Speed Insights will automatically start collecting data

3. **View Performance Data**:
   - After deployment and user visits, access the Speed Insights dashboard
   - Performance metrics will be available after sufficient traffic

